{"agent":"lane-autosync","data":{"by":"lane-autosync","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":2,"detail":"`_auto_sync_on_claim` only sets `wt.sync_note` when the automatic-sync outcome has `status == \"conflict\"`. The `auto_sync` contract in `sync.py` says a `refused` outcome also leaves the tree as it was and “says why” (for example, when `[worktree] auto_sync_refuse_on_conflict` is enabled and the merge/rebase would conflict). For that outcome the claim sets no note, so the claim can succeed with an empty `sync_warn` and start the item on an unsynced tree, silently leaving the gate baseline problem this change is meant to report.","digest":"3890d462856bec1c","location":"ddflow/api/lifecycle/claim.py:_auto_sync_on_claim","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/api/lifecycle/claim.py:_auto_sync_on_claim"},{"chunk":4,"detail":"`usable()` only rejects a tree whose resolved path equals the resolved `repo` path. Git commands run with `tree` as the working directory affect the containing worktree, so a path inside the primary checkout passes the guard: with `repo = Path(\"/repo\")` and `tree = Path(\"/repo/ddflow\")`, `is_primary()` returns False because the paths differ, `git -C /repo/ddflow rev-parse --git-dir` succeeds, and `usable()` returns True. Auto-sync can then run `git -C /repo/ddflow merge main` or `rebase main`, modifying the primary checkout despite the stated “never touches the primary checkout” invariant. The check should use the worktree top-level (`git rev-parse --show-toplevel`) or otherwise ensure `tree` is not inside the primary checkout.","digest":"1bf58e057a24e52c","location":"ddflow/services/autosync.py:usable/is_primary","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/services/autosync.py:usable/is_primary"},{"chunk":4,"detail":"When a rebase fails with conflicts and `git rebase --abort` also fails, `_failed_rebase()` records `out.aborted = False` and returns a conflict/refused status. `autosync.blocks()` ignores `aborted` and only stops the gate for `status == \"conflict\"` when `auto_sync_refuse_on_conflict` is true. Thus, with that knob false (or when `files` is empty and the status is `refused`), `before_gate` can start gates in a worktree that `_failed_rebase()` itself says may be left mid-rebase. A failed abort should block the gate regardless of the conflict-refusal setting.","digest":"fdfb0d2fa1279b74","location":"ddflow/services/branchsync.py:_failed_rebase","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/services/branchsync.py:_failed_rebase"}],"chunks_total":6,"coverage":"4/6 chunk(s) reviewed","diff_sha":"e49bcb97d04921dbbc28a2e39fb7554ac9674fc4bf082f91ebee1b5704b07ce0","diff_stat":{"deletions":0,"files":0,"insertions":0,"untracked":0},"max_chunk_chars":5000,"output_digest":"93a4561d7ff84f8d","output_file":".ddflow/local/reviews/GM-auto-sync-main.rubber_duck.[REDACTED:name].20261113T033723Z-41ab9e96.jsonl","review_kind":"delta","reviewed":[2,3,4,5],"reviewer":"[REDACTED:name]","reviewer_digest":"3926c0df5644d7de","status":"PARTIAL","terminated_by":"SIGTERM","tree_sha":"9c4301bf7fa7+clean","wanted":[1,2,3,4,5,6]},"gate":"rubber_duck","reason":"the review was terminated by SIGTERM mid-round after 4 chunk(s) were reviewed (2, 3, 4, 5); those findings are checkpointed, the remaining chunks were not reviewed, which is not a pass"},"id":"ee6602e93fa76a84148e0d470","kind":"gate.partial","lamport":188994,"schema":1,"subject":"GM-auto-sync-main","ts":"2026-11-13T03:47:08.199977Z"}
